{
  "info": {
    "name": "Seat Reserve API",
    "description": "Seat reservation service (Paytm Money take-home).\n\n**One collection, two targets.** Set the collection variable `target` to `live` (the Render deployment) or `local` (`http://localhost:8080`, e.g. after `docker compose up`). A collection-level script picks the matching URL and admin key before every request, and clears saved tokens and ids when the target changes.\n\n**Setup:** for `live`, paste the admin key from the submission email into `liveAdminKey`. `local` works out of the box (`local-admin-key`, the docker-compose default).\n\n**Run:** Collection Runner, in order. Folder 1 saves the tokens, folder 2 creates a fresh show, folders 3 and 4 walk through every rule (seat taken, idempotent replay, key reuse, per-user limit, token identity, hold -> confirm, cancel) with a test on each response.\n\nFor the 20k-request concurrency burst use `./burst.sh <BASE_URL>` from the repo; Postman runs requests one at a time.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "target",
      "value": "live",
      "description": "live or local: picks the URL and admin key below."
    },
    {
      "key": "liveUrl",
      "value": "https://seat-reserve-lrvt.onrender.com"
    },
    {
      "key": "liveAdminKey",
      "value": "",
      "description": "From the submission email (never committed)."
    },
    {
      "key": "localUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080"
    },
    {
      "key": "localAdminKey",
      "value": "local-admin-key",
      "description": "The docker-compose / dev default."
    },
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "{{liveUrl}}",
      "description": "Set automatically from target before every request."
    },
    {
      "key": "adminKey",
      "value": "{{liveAdminKey}}",
      "description": "Set automatically from target before every request."
    },
    {
      "key": "adminToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "aliceToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "bobToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "showId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "aliceKey",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "aliceReservationId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "bobHoldId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "lastTarget",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Switch environments by changing the `target` variable: live | local.",
          "const target = String(pm.variables.get('target') || 'live').trim().toLowerCase();",
          "if (!['live', 'local'].includes(target)) {",
          "    throw new Error(`target must be 'live' or 'local', got '${target}'`);",
          "}",
          "pm.variables.set('baseUrl', pm.variables.get(`${target}Url`));",
          "pm.variables.set('adminKey', pm.variables.get(`${target}AdminKey`));",
          "// Tokens and ids from the other target are useless here (different signing secret, different",
          "// database): forget them when the target changes, so folder 1 and 2 start clean.",
          "if (pm.collectionVariables.get('lastTarget') !== target) {",
          "    ['adminToken', 'aliceToken', 'bobToken', 'showId', 'aliceKey', 'aliceReservationId', 'bobHoldId']",
          "        .forEach(v => pm.collectionVariables.set(v, ''));",
          "    pm.collectionVariables.set('lastTarget', target);",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Health & metrics",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Liveness",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health/live",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health",
                "live"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Process is up. Does not touch the database."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Readiness",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health/ready",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "health",
                "ready"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Ready to serve: checks Postgres (fails closed). The first call after idle may take ~30-60 s while the free Render instance wakes up."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Prometheus metrics",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/actuator/prometheus",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "actuator",
                "prometheus"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Scrape endpoint. Look for reservations_confirmed_total, reservations_declined_total{reason}, seats_available/held/confirmed/capacity{show}, reservation_latency_seconds."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. Auth (run first)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Admin token",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Admin-Key",
                "value": "{{adminKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/token",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "token"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Admin token: needs the X-Admin-Key header (liveAdminKey or localAdminKey, picked by target). Its scope includes `admin`, which POST /shows requires.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"user_id\": \"admin\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"adminToken\", pm.response.json().access_token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Alice token",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/token",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "token"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Signed JWT for user `alice`. Single user tokens are open (no admin key); the identity used by every reserve call comes from this token, never from the request body.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"user_id\": \"alice\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"aliceToken\", pm.response.json().access_token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Bob token",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/token",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "token"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Signed JWT for user `bob`. Single user tokens are open (no admin key); the identity used by every reserve call comes from this token, never from the request body.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"user_id\": \"bob\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"bobToken\", pm.response.json().access_token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Bulk tokens (admin)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "X-Admin-Key",
                "value": "{{adminKey}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/tokens",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "tokens"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Mint many user tokens in one call (max 25,000), for load tests. Either `count` (+ optional `prefix`, default `user-`) or an explicit `user_ids` list. Admin key required.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"count\": 3,\n  \"prefix\": \"buyer-\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"3 tokens\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().count).to.eql(3));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Shows",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create show (admin)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{adminToken}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/shows",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "shows"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Creates a fresh show with 10 seats and a per-user limit of 4. Saves `showId` for the requests below. Run this before folder 3 so every run starts from a clean show.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Postman demo\",\n  \"seats\": [\n    \"A1\",\n    \"A2\",\n    \"A3\",\n    \"A4\",\n    \"A5\",\n    \"A6\",\n    \"A7\",\n    \"A8\",\n    \"A9\",\n    \"A10\"\n  ],\n  \"price_paise\": 25000,\n  \"per_user_limit\": 4\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 201\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"showId\", pm.response.json().id);",
                  "pm.test(\"10 seats available\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().counts.available).to.eql(10));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Create show as a normal user (403)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{aliceToken}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/shows",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "shows"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Only tokens with the admin scope can create shows.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"should fail\",\n  \"seats\": [\n    \"A1\"\n  ],\n  \"price_paise\": 100\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 403\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(403));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get show (public)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/shows/{{showId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "shows",
                "{{showId}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Public, no token. Returns every seat's status and the counts; the invariant available + held + confirmed == total always holds."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const c = pm.response.json().counts;",
                  "pm.test(\"invariant: available + held + confirmed == total\", () => pm.expect(c.available + c.held + c.confirmed).to.eql(c.total));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Reserve: the rules",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Alice reserves A1 (201)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{aliceToken}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/shows/{{showId}}/reserve",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "shows",
                "{{showId}}",
                "reserve"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Confirms immediately. A fresh idempotency key is generated before the request and saved as `aliceKey`. The key may also be sent as an `Idempotency-Key` header (if both are sent they must match).",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"seats\": [\n    \"A1\"\n  ],\n  \"idempotency_key\": \"{{aliceKey}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('aliceKey', pm.variables.replaceIn('{{$guid}}'));"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 201\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"aliceReservationId\", pm.response.json().reservation_id);",
                  "pm.test(\"confirmed\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql(\"confirmed\"));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Alice retries with the same key (200 replay)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{aliceToken}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/shows/{{showId}}/reserve",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "shows",
                "{{showId}}",
                "reserve"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Same key + same body = the original reservation again, with 200 and `Idempotent-Replayed: true`. No second sale.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"seats\": [\n    \"A1\"\n  ],\n  \"idempotency_key\": \"{{aliceKey}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"Idempotent-Replayed: true\", () => pm.response.to.have.header(\"Idempotent-Replayed\", \"true\"));",
                  "pm.test(\"same reservation\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().reservation_id).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get(\"aliceReservationId\")));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Alice reuses the key for different seats (409)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{aliceToken}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/shows/{{showId}}/reserve",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "shows",
                "{{showId}}",
                "reserve"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Same key, different body: rejected, so a key can never silently mean two different purchases.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"seats\": [\n    \"A2\"\n  ],\n  \"idempotency_key\": \"{{aliceKey}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 409\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));",
                  "pm.test(\"error code IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error.code).to.eql(\"IDEMPOTENCY_KEY_REUSED\"));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Bob tries A1 (409 seat taken)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{bobToken}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/shows/{{showId}}/reserve",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "shows",
                "{{showId}}",
                "reserve"
              ]
            },
            "description": "The seat is Alice's. Under a burst, exactly one request per seat gets 201 and every other gets this.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"seats\": [\n    \"A1\"\n  ],\n  \"idempotency_key\": \"{{$guid}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 409\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));",
                  "pm.test(\"error code SEAT_TAKEN\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error.code).to.eql(\"SEAT_TAKEN\"));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Alice asks for 4 more (409 per-user limit)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{aliceToken}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/shows/{{showId}}/reserve",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "shows",
                "{{showId}}",
                "reserve"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Alice already has 1 seat; 4 more would make 5 > per_user_limit 4. All-or-nothing: none are taken.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"seats\": [\n    \"A4\",\n    \"A5\",\n    \"A6\",\n    \"A7\"\n  ],\n  \"idempotency_key\": \"{{$guid}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 409\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(409));",
                  "pm.test(\"error code PER_USER_LIMIT\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error.code).to.eql(\"PER_USER_LIMIT\"));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Bob spoofs user_id in the body (ignored)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{bobToken}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/shows/{{showId}}/reserve",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "shows",
                "{{showId}}",
                "reserve"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Identity comes from the token only; the `user_id` field is ignored, so the reservation is Bob's.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"seats\": [\n    \"A8\"\n  ],\n  \"user_id\": \"alice\",\n  \"idempotency_key\": \"{{$guid}}\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 201\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test(\"owned by bob\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().user_id).to.eql(\"bob\"));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Unknown seat (400)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{bobToken}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/shows/{{showId}}/reserve",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "shows",
                "{{showId}}",
                "reserve"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Seats that don't exist in the show are a client error.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"seats\": [\n    \"Z99\"\n  ]\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 400\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(400));",
                  "pm.test(\"error code UNKNOWN_SEATS\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().error.code).to.eql(\"UNKNOWN_SEATS\"));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "No token (401)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/shows/{{showId}}/reserve",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "shows",
                "{{showId}}",
                "reserve"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Reserving requires a signed JWT.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"seats\": [\n    \"A9\"\n  ]\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"status 401\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Raw user id instead of a JWT (401)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer alice"
              },
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/shows/{{showId}}/reserve",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "shows",
